0094: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0095:     """
0096:     Replace the active black cutout's tail with background and mark the cutout side facing a colored source region.
0097: 
0098:     Input structure:
0099:     - The dominant color is background, with black rectangle-plus-tail cutouts, one gray source region, and colored distractors.
0100:     - Non-gray colored regions and single pixels are distractors/blockers, even when they are multi-pixel staircase shapes.
0101: 
0102:     Rule:
0103:     - Find each black cutout whose largest solid rectangle leaves exactly a two-pixel tail.
0104:     - The active gray source region is visible only by horizontal rays through background from a cutout's left or right side.
0105:     - Select the unique cutout side with the most same-source visible rows, erase that cutout's tail to background, and recolor the full selected vertical side pink (6).
0106: 
0107:     Key insight:
