0061: 
0062:     Rule
0063:     Delete the all-background separator columns. Keep the first group in its original vertical position, then process the remaining groups from left to right: shift each group vertically, without rotation or recoloring, so its left endpoint is on the same row as the previous placed group's right endpoint, and paste it immediately to the right.
0064: 
0065:     Key insight
0066:     The intended contacts are the degree-1 edge endpoints, not every possible foreground edge overlap, which makes the packed strip a single connected chain.
0067:     """
0068:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
